  "description": "Contract law covers when agreements become enforceable, what their terms mean, and what can happen when someone does not keep a promise. You’ll look at how contracts are formed, what can affect whether they hold up, and common ways disputes are handled, using examples like leases, job offers, freelance work, and app terms. Rules can vary by state.",
  "landingPage": {
    "audience": [
      "Renters reviewing a lease before signing",
      "Workers weighing a job offer or employment agreement",
      "Freelancers and small-business owners who sign agreements",
      "Consumers trying to make sense of app terms and online agreements"
    ],
    "outcomes": [
      "Tell when an offer and acceptance can make a promise enforceable.",
      "Read leases, job offers, app terms, and freelance agreements for renewal, termination, and liability terms.",
      "Spot circumstances that may make an agreement unenforceable or change what it means.",
      "Explain what can happen when someone breaks an agreement and what a court may award.",
      "Describe common ways contract disputes are handled and when to ask a lawyer."
    ],
    "valueProposition": "Read everyday agreements and spot terms that could limit your choices or leave you owing money."
  }
}

